# NOTICE — what the MIT license in this repository covers

The [LICENSE](LICENSE) file is the unmodified MIT license text, so that
automated license detection (GitHub, `licensee`, SBOM scanners) resolves it to
`MIT` rather than to `Other`. This file carries the scope note that used to be
appended to it.

**Covered by MIT:** the ecosystem content authored in this repository —
registry manifests, first-party skills, agents, workflows, MCP server
manifests, knowledge packs, documentation, examples, and the repo tooling under
`scripts/` and `packages/`.

**Not covered, and not vendored here:** third-party items referenced by
manifest (see [`registry/`](registry/)). Each declares its upstream repository
and a pinned tag or commit SHA, and remains under its own upstream license —
this repository does not copy their code. The license of every referenced item
is declared in its `marblo.yaml` and printed in the catalog table in
[README.md](README.md).

**Also not covered:** the Marblo desktop application itself. The orchestration
engine is closed source and distributed under its own terms — see
[README.md](README.md#whats-open-and-what-isnt).

**First-party exceptions.** Two first-party knowledge packs are CC-BY-4.0
rather than MIT, declared in their own manifests:
[`knowledge/fleet-operations`](knowledge/fleet-operations/) and
[`knowledge/curated-llm-resources`](knowledge/curated-llm-resources/). Where an
item's `marblo.yaml` declares a license, that declaration wins; where nothing is
declared, MIT applies.
